  "result": "Excellent! All 75 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT support to the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **Added `lineVAT(line)` function** in `src/invoices.js`:\n   - Calculates VAT on the line amount **after discount**: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) * vatRate / 100`\n   - Uses `roundCents()` for proper banker's rounding per line\n   - Clamps at 0 (no negative VAT)\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)`** to return:\n   ```javascript\n   {\n     subtotal,       // sum of line totals\n     discount,       // sum of line discounts\n     vat,           // sum of rounded per-line VATs\n     total          // subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **Updated `renderInvoiceText(invoice)`** to:\n   - Display VAT line only if `vat > 0`\n   - Place VAT line just above the total\n\n**Key design points:**\n- VAT is calculated **per line** on the amount after discount, then rounded per line, then summed (not calculated as percentage of invoice total)\n- Supports all VAT rates from the catalogue: 21%, 9%, 0%\n- Amounts never go below zero (VAT is clamped)\n- VAT-exempt items (0% rate) don't show a VAT line\n\n**Tests verify:**\n- VAT calculation on discounted amounts\n- Per-line rounding of VAT\n- Different VAT rates\n- VAT-exempt items\n- VAT clamping when discount exceeds line total\n- Proper invoice rendering with VAT line\n\nAll 75 tests pass.",
